-- Sharing metadata: read by tooling and the manager detail pane.
return {
  summary = "A Ruby/Sapphire-style box screen: a grid you can see, a cursor that carries a Pokemon, and a way to find one of two hundred and forty.",
  author = "MadeinTaly",
  -- shown in the manager's detail pane next to the author
  support = "https://linktr.ee/made_in_taly",
  tags = { "ui", "storage", "quality-of-life", "boxes" },
  compat = { modApi = 2 },
  differences = {
    added = {
      "GRID BIG: a 320x288 surface through the engine's own uiSize hook -- battle pics at scale 1 instead of half, and a palette zone per cell so every Pokemon in the grid wears its own species colours, twenty-one at once where the Game Boy could show four",
      "BOX HEALS (off by default): closing the screen rests everything in storage -- full HP, status cleared, PP restored -- through Pokemon.heal, the same routine the Pokemon Centre nurse calls",
      "a BOXES row on the start menu and under the Pokemon Center PC's own box row, opening a 5x4 grid of the current box",
      "an OPEN FROM option choosing which of those two entrances exist: START+PC, START, or PC",
      "a cursor that picks a Pokemon up with A and puts it down with A, swapping when the target slot is taken",
      "START over a Pokemon opens the game's own summary screen, which recalculates a box mon's stats on the way in",
      "walking off the left or right edge of a box steps to the next one; B is back from anywhere and only back",
      "SELECT crosses to the party and back, which is how a mon is deposited or withdrawn",
      "a HEADER ROW: UP out of the top row lands on the box title, where A opens the BOX MENU and LEFT/RIGHT change box",
      "FIND: search every box from the cursor forward by species substring, by type or by mark, wrapping back to where it started; START on the header is FIND NEXT",
      "JUMP TO BOX: the twelve boxes with their names and how full each one is, without the vanilla PC's save prompt",
      "SORT: BY DEX, BY LEVEL (strongest first), BY NAME or BY TYPE, stable, in place, and UNDO for the last one while the screen is open",
      "MARKS: Gen 3's circle, square, triangle and heart, stored on the Pokemon and drawn in the corner of its cell; MARK MODE is how they are set",
      "NAME BOX: eight glyphs through the engine's own naming screen, stored in the save rather than the install",
      "WALLPAPER: a pattern and a four-colour palette per box, including NIGHT, which is the greys in reverse and therefore a real dark mode",
      "PLACE CRY (on by default): the cry of whichever Pokemon just landed in a slot",
      "OW SPRITES (experimental prerelease, off by default): when Wilds of Kanto (overworld_wild_spawns) is installed and enabled, draws its per-species overworld sprite in each occupied CLASSIC cell instead of the half-scale battle picture, reached through mod.find rather than a manifest dependency, so it changes nothing for anyone without that mod",
    },
    changed = {
      "the grid draws each Pokemon's battle pic at half scale, because Gen 1 has only four generic party icons and a grid of those is unreadable",
      "with CURSOR WRAP on, UP from the top row now stops on the header instead of wrapping; UP again wraps to the bottom as before, so the wrap is not lost, it gains a stop",
      "a Pokemon withdrawn from a box into the party has its stat block recalculated, which the vanilla PC always did and this screen did not -- a mon decoded out of an imported .sav could reach the party menu with no stats at all",
    },
    known = {
      "BOX HEALS runs once on close rather than per placement, because a swap is a deposit and a withdrawal at the same time and a move between two box slots is neither; and it covers every box, not only the open one",
      "BOX HEALS leaves the party alone -- you can still deposit six and take them straight back, but the party is the half of this screen that is not storage",
      "a box stays a COMPACT array, the shape src/pokemon/Boxes.lua and the save format use, so dropping into an empty cell appends to the end instead of leaving a hole -- Ruby's sparse grid is the one thing not reproduced",
      "the vanilla box PC is left in place and still works whichever way OPEN FROM is set; this is an additional entrance, not a replacement for Bill's PC",
      "pics come through Assets.image, so a sprite mod's art shows up here too",
      "the party may not be emptied, exactly as the vanilla PC refuses the last mon",
      "FIND searches storage and not the party, because the party is six visible slots on the same screen",
      "marks are drawn as shapes rather than glyphs, because the Gen 1 font has none; they are stored as a four-character string on the Pokemon and travel with the save",
      "a wallpaper's colours reach the whole surface only in BIG: a CLASSIC cell is three and a half tiles, and half a tile cannot carry a palette zone, so CLASSIC gets the pattern alone",
      "an empty confirm on the naming screen keeps the name a box already has -- the engine treats what you pass it as the fallback for an empty confirm, not as a pre-filled grid, so typing the plain BOX n back is what returns a box to being numbered",
      "every wallpaper colour is authored in this mod's own source; no ROM palette is copied, and modkit lint still reports no ROM-derived content",
      "OW SPRITES only applies in GRID CLASSIC; GRID BIG keeps the battle picture, because its 56px cell already draws one at scale 1 and a 16px overworld sprite would have to be enlarged to fill it",
      "OW SPRITES treats a black-silhouette fallback from the other mod as a miss and falls back to the battle picture, because a silhouette in a storage grid hides which Pokemon it is and the battle picture does not",
    },
  },
}
